-- title:
--   Ordinary eigenline at p in weight 2, p odd
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, $N \ge 1$ with $p \nmid N$, and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \notin S$; let $k = 2$ be the weight, carried as an integer $k$ together with a natural number $kn$ with $(kn : \mathbb{Z}) = k$ (so that the exponent $kn - 1$ below, natural subtraction, equals $1$). Let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$ and $\theta : \mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\ N\ k\ S \to F$ a ring homomorphism from the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$), with $\theta(T_p) \neq 0$. Let $\rho : \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a monoid homomorphism which is trivial on the elements fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ pointwise; assume that for every nonzero $u \in F^2$ some $\sigma$ carries $u$ outside the line $F \cdot u$, and that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \ne p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$ (i.e. $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$), one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma) = \theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell^{kn-1}$ in $F$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $P$. Then: first, for every such $\ell$, $A$ and Frobenius $\sigma$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell^{kn-1}$; and second, there is a nonzero $v \in F^2$ such that the line $F \cdot v$ is stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, every $\sigma$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ satisfies $\rho(\sigma)w - w \in F \cdot v$ for all $w \in F^2$, every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $p$ for $P$ satisfies $\rho(\sigma)w - \theta(T_p)\,w \in F \cdot v$ for all $w$, and every inertia element $\sigma$ acting on the $p$-th roots of unity by $\mu \mapsto \mu^{a}$ satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v = a^{kn-1}\,v$.
--
--   This is the ordinarity at $p$ of a mod-$p$ two-dimensional representation whose Frobenius traces and determinants come from a Hecke eigensystem of weight $2$ with non-zero $T_p$-eigenvalue: the existence of a decomposition-stable line on which inertia acts by the $(k-1)$-st power of the mod-$p$ cyclotomic character, with unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by $\theta(T_p)$. It is the weight $2$ instance of the statement, used alongside its weight $3$ counterpart.
